Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='tworoots', at=datetime(2026, 9, 14, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The instance file has two roots, CodeRoot and DataRoot; the data lives in the private data repository', body="*THE INSTANCE FILE HAS TWO ROOTS, NOT ONE* (2026-09-14, chain `datasplit`, `docs/DATASPLIT-PLAN-2026-09-14.md`, ARCHITECTURE §10.7): `repo` (the code checkout) and `data` (the instance file's own directory by default) are two types, `CodeRoot`/`DataRoot`, so a new path in `instance.toml` declares its side rather than inheriting the checkout. `SUZATARY_INSTANCE` is the one env var every job — the CLI, the units, `hourly-triage.sh`, `safe-push.sh` — carries to find both roots, and `safe-push.sh` REFUSES to run without it rather than silently skip the live tests it gates on. *MIGRATED 2026-09-26*: the chains, `state.json`, `briefings/`, `notes/`, `mbsyncrc` and this box's `instance.toml` live in the PRIVATE data repository, checked out beside this one; its instance names both roots absolutely, and `instance.toml` in this checkout is an IGNORED LINK to it, so a command run here reads the same deployment the units do. `safe-push.sh` resolves the data tree with `realpath` through that link and commits the agent's writes there; nothing data-shaped is committed to the code repository again (the `.gitignore` names every data path). Its history still holds the data, so a public code repository is a fresh clone (plan §9). The data tree's literal path lives ONLY in the nixos config repository (`services.suzatary.userRepo` and the briefing and main-session units); the public-tree guard forbids a home path in any tracked file — reach for `$SUZATARY_REPO`/`$SUZATARY_INSTANCE` or the module's options, never a hand-typed path.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-14 (chain datasplit, docs/DATASPLIT-PLAN-2026-09-14.md, ARCHITECTURE §10.7); migrated 2026-09-26.', supersedes=()))